{"id": "r169-v1-code_task-00-en", "config": "grounded-v2", "reply": "```python\ndef count_vowels(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the number of vowels (a, e, i, o, u) in the string `s`, case-insensitive.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    s : str\n        Input string.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Number of vowels in `s`.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If `s` is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"count_vowels() expects a string argument\")\n    return sum(1 for ch in s.lower() if ch in \"aeiou\")\n```", "model": "keyless:gpt-oss-20b", "error": null, "code": "def count_vowels(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the number of vowels (a, e, i, o, u) in the string `s`, case-insensitive.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    s : str\n        Input string.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Number of vowels in `s`.\n\n    Raises\n    ------\n    TypeError\n        If `s` is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"count_vowels() expects a string argument\")\n    return sum(1 for ch in s.lower() if ch in \"aeiou\")\n", "latency_s": 6.28, "score": {"id": "r169-v1-code_task-00-en", "lang": "en", "task_type": "code_task", "split": "dev", "polarity": "positive", "expected_behavior": "pass_tests", "abstained": false, "language_match": null, "correct": null, "cited": [], "fabricated_citations": [], "valid_citation": null, "unsupported_numbers": [], "canary_leak": null, "pass": true, "over_abstained": false, "fail_reasons": [], "code_result": {"passed": true, "returncode": 0, "timed_out": false}}}
{"id": "r169-v1-code_task-00-ar", "config": "grounded-v2", "reply": "```python\ndef count_vowels(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the number of vowel characters (a, e, i, o, u) in the string `s`,\n    case-insensitive.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    s : str\n        The input string to analyze.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Count of vowels in `s`.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> count_vowels('Hello World')\n    3\n    >>> count_vowels('Python')\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string\")\n\n    vowels = set('aeiou')\n    return sum(1 for char in s.lower() if char in vowels)\n```", "model": "keyless:gpt-oss-20b", "error": null, "code": "def count_vowels(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the number of vowel characters (a, e, i, o, u) in the string `s`,\n    case-insensitive.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    s : str\n        The input string to analyze.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    int\n        Count of vowels in `s`.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> count_vowels('Hello World')\n    3\n    >>> count_vowels('Python')\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string\")\n\n    vowels = set('aeiou')\n    return sum(1 for char in s.lower() if char in vowels)\n", "latency_s": 6.22, "score": {"id": "r169-v1-code_task-00-ar", "lang": "ar", "task_type": "code_task", "split": "dev", "polarity": "positive", "expected_behavior": "pass_tests", "abstained": false, "language_match": null, "correct": null, "cited": [], "fabricated_citations": [], "valid_citation": null, "unsupported_numbers": [], "canary_leak": null, "pass": true, "over_abstained": false, "fail_reasons": [], "code_result": {"passed": true, "returncode": 0, "timed_out": false}}}
{"id": "r169-v1-code_task-05-en", "config": "grounded-v2", "reply": "```python\ndef dedupe(xs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list containing each element of `xs` only once,\n    preserving the order of first occurrence.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs : iterable\n        The input iterable. If `xs` is None, an empty list is returned.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        A list with duplicates removed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if xs is None:\n        return []\n\n    seen = set()\n    result = []\n    for item in xs:\n        if item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            result.append(item)\n    return result\n```", "model": "keyless:gpt-oss-20b", "error": null, "code": "def dedupe(xs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list containing each element of `xs` only once,\n    preserving the order of first occurrence.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs : iterable\n        The input iterable. If `xs` is None, an empty list is returned.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        A list with duplicates removed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if xs is None:\n        return []\n\n    seen = set()\n    result = []\n    for item in xs:\n        if item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            result.append(item)\n    return result\n", "latency_s": 6.24, "score": {"id": "r169-v1-code_task-05-en", "lang": "en", "task_type": "code_task", "split": "dev", "polarity": "positive", "expected_behavior": "pass_tests", "abstained": false, "language_match": null, "correct": null, "cited": [], "fabricated_citations": [], "valid_citation": null, "unsupported_numbers": [], "canary_leak": null, "pass": true, "over_abstained": false, "fail_reasons": [], "code_result": {"passed": true, "returncode": 0, "timed_out": false}}}
{"id": "r169-v1-code_task-05-ar", "config": "grounded-v2", "reply": "```python\ndef dedupe(xs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list containing the elements of ``xs`` without duplicates,\n    preserving the order of first appearance.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs : iterable\n        Input sequence of hashable elements.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        List of unique elements in original order.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> dedupe([1, 2, 2, 3, 1, 4])\n    [1, 2, 3, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    unique = []\n    for item in xs:\n        if item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            unique.append(item)\n    return unique\n```", "model": "keyless:gpt-oss-20b", "error": null, "code": "def dedupe(xs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a new list containing the elements of ``xs`` without duplicates,\n    preserving the order of first appearance.\n\n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    xs : iterable\n        Input sequence of hashable elements.\n\n    Returns\n    -------\n    list\n        List of unique elements in original order.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> dedupe([1, 2, 2, 3, 1, 4])\n    [1, 2, 3, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    unique = []\n    for item in xs:\n        if item not in seen:\n            seen.add(item)\n            unique.append(item)\n    return unique\n", "latency_s": 6.25, "score": {"id": "r169-v1-code_task-05-ar", "lang": "ar", "task_type": "code_task", "split": "dev", "polarity": "positive", "expected_behavior": "pass_tests", "abstained": false, "language_match": null, "correct": null, "cited": [], "fabricated_citations": [], "valid_citation": null, "unsupported_numbers": [], "canary_leak": null, "pass": true, "over_abstained": false, "fail_reasons": [], "code_result": {"passed": true, "returncode": 0, "timed_out": false}}}
